# Comparison result as a condition

Verifies an `if` consumes the boolean produced by a comparison. Each body runs
only when its relation holds, so the true relations print while the false ones
leave no output.

>>> source
const a: int = 3
const b: int = 5

if (a < b) {
    print(1)
}

if (a > b) {
    print(2)
}

if (a == b) {
    print(3)
}

if (a != b) {
    print(4)
}

<<< stdout
1
4

<<< stderr
